  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Steps to reproduce:\n\n1. Create gameobject with VRC_SyncVideoStream component.\n2. Create gameobject with VRC_VideoSpeaker component referencing VRC_SyncVideoStream and Channel Type set to \"Stereo_Mix\", and AudioSource component on same gameobject with Spatial Blend turned to 1 (3D) and Spatialize checked, and ONSP AudioSource component with \"Spatialization Enabled\" checked\n3. Add gameobject with Reverb Zone component covering the area around the AudioSource\n\nExpected:\nThe audio plays back with the reverb affect applied and is additionally spatialized.\n\nActual:\nThe audio has no reverb applied but is spatialized.\n\nAdditional detail:\nIf the \"spatial blend\" is set back to 0 (2D), but \"spatialize\" and \"spatialize enabled\" in the ONSP component are still enabled, the sound remains spatialized but without reverb.\nIf \"Spatialize\" and \"spatialize enabled\" are unchecked, then the reverb effect is applied, but spatialization is not (obviously, I suppose).\nAlso, adding the \"Reverb Filter\" component directly to the gameobject with the audio source turns off spatialization, but also fails to apply the reverb effect.\n\nThis problem seems unique to the audio sources driven by VRC_VideoSpeaker component. A regular audiosource just playing an audio clip receives both reverb and spatialization effects just fine.\n\n",
